/**
 * ShareNet Conformance Vector Generator
 *
 * Source: 06-CONFORMANCE-AND-AI-MODEL.md §A2 (structure), §A4 (required suites)
 *
 * This is THE reference generator. Per the conformance architecture (§A2):
 *   "Rule: exactly one generator. Vectors are generated by the reference
 *    implementation and committed. Other implementations consume them and
 *    may never regenerate them. A generator per language reproduces the
 *    failure this suite exists to prevent."
 *
 * In a production ShareNet repo this generator would be Rust (the reference
 * implementation language). In this Next.js sandbox we use TypeScript as
 * the reference. The vectors themselves are language-independent JSON, so
 * a Rust generator would produce byte-identical vectors given the same
 * deterministic inputs and keys.
 *
 * CRITICAL: every vector contains REAL cryptographic values — real Ed25519
 * signatures, real CBOR bytes, real Merkle roots, real NodeIds. NO
 * placeholders, NO zero signatures, NO `sha256(label)` shortcuts. This is
 * the direct fix for audit finding 00-AUDIT.md §3.3 (golden vectors were
 * `sha256("cbor-manifest-0")` with all-zero signatures).
 *
 * Run: `bun run scripts/generate-vectors.ts`
 * Output: /public/conformance/vectors/*.json
 */

